# QA harness output and its throwaway Chrome profile.

# Agent-fleet orchestration. Kept local: these reference absolute paths into the
# operational vault and the AKP passport, and they drive a private model fleet.
# The repository publishes the lab, its evidence harness and the run contract.
night.py
run-night.cmd
plan-night.mjs
logs/

# Capture output from ANY lane, not just the default directory. A lane wrote to
# qa/captures-N1/ with its own Chrome profile inside, and the narrower
# `qa/captures/` rule let thousands of profile files into `git add -A`.

# Lane scratch. Lanes spawn their own Chrome profiles and debug scripts; without
# these, `git add -A` stages tens of thousands of profile files.
s4u-probe.cmd
launch-lanes.cmd

# Any Chrome profile any harness makes, whatever it is called.

plan-rooms.mjs

# qa/ is a WHITELIST, not a pattern list.
#
# Four separate Chrome profile directories reached the index under four names a
# pattern rule did not anticipate: .chrome-profile-*, captures-N1/, tmp-deep/,
# and .profile-<pid>-<rand>/. Each time the fix was a narrower pattern and each
# time the next tool invented a new name. Ignore everything under qa/ and name
# the handful of files that belong in the repository.
qa/*
!qa/capture.mjs
!qa/room-shot.mjs
!qa/chrome-lifecycle.mjs
!qa/package.json
!qa/package-lock.json

__pycache__/
*.pyc
